2:player

172:In Bamboo Cloud's attic, I stand at the door to Fuuka Minami's private lounge, recalling my conversation with Ume.
173:The boss wants to see me at this hour? Should I be worried?
174:Ume
175:Perhaps she's pleased with your work and wants to have a chat with you.
176:Don't overthink it. Being invited for a chat isn't necessarily a bad thing.
177:Is there anything I should watch out for?
178:Nothing beyond the usual. Well, actually... there is something you should keep in mind.
179:Ms. Fuuka was in a good mood today and had a bit too much to drink. If she tries anything, don't let her take it too far.
180:I... can say "no" to the boss?
181:Of course you can, hehe. Middle managers must learn not only downward management... but upward management as well.
182:Learning when to rebuff unreasonable demands from the boss is just one more workplace lesson for you to learn.
183:Now go. Don't keep Ms. Fuuka waiting.
184:"Knock, knock..." I rap at the door and realize that it's open.
185:Fuuka Minami
186:Come in.
187:The room is bathed in a warm, yellow light. Draped over a chaise longue by the window, Fuuka Minami gives me a cursory wave when she sees me come in.
188:Have a seat.
189:Boss...
190:Drink?
191:Before I can respond, she sits up and slides a cup of wine over to me. The clear liquid inside smells faintly of osmanthus.
193:Accept
195:Decline
196:Oh, sure.
197:Bottoms up.
198:Remember Ume's advice about "upward management."
199:Sorry, Boss, but I'm not much of a drinker.
200:What? That's a serious problem in business. But that's fine, I can teach you.
201:She sits up and leans in until the wine cup held between her slender fingers stops right in front of me.
202:Well? Aren't you going to take it? Or did you want me to pour it into your mouth myself?
203:Her voice drops, as if she's slightly displeased.
204:Stand your ground
205:Sensing that my boss is about to get angry, I have no choice but to drink.
206:"Upward management... Upward management... Upward management..." Repeating this mantra to myself in my head, I hold firm.
207:I'm serious, Ms. Fuuka. I don't drink.
208:Hehe, well done.
209:I can't believe you didn't budge an inch.
210:That was unnecessary...
211:Sitting right down next to me, Fuuka gets me into a chokehold with one arm and raises the cup to my lips with her other hand.
212:Now that I'm giving you a helping hand, you should be able to drink... right?
213:My mission is before me, and my boss' orders mixed with threats are in my ear.
214:Adamantly refuse!
215:I accept my fate. I reach out, take the cup, and down its contents.
216:Please, Ume! Save me in my time of need!
217:I'm serious, Boss! I don't drink.
218:(whisper) Tch, you're no fun.
219:Her enthusiasm perhaps worn down at last by my firm resolve, she gives up on trying to make me drink. She leans against me with a sigh and twiddles the cup between her fingers.
220:The vague fragrance next to me mixed with the pungent smell of the wine is practically giving me second-hand intoxication.
221:Um... How much have you had to drink?
222:Hm... A little? No, wait... maybe a little more than a little.
223:Boss, are you... drunk?
224:Me? Maybe a little. But I can still remember who you are and that I had Ume send you here, so relax.
225:When she tilts her head to the side, Fuuka's face flushes reddish--. Looks like she's more than just "a little" drunk.
226:Right! I asked you to come... and you came.
227:She stands up and walks over to the open window. The moon shines brightly in the sky while the lights below shimmer in the darkness. I know that those lights are from Bamboo Cloud's celebration, where they're shining on countless smiling faces.
228:What do you see?
229:Bamboo Cloud's celebration... It's so grand and lively.
230:And?
231:Uh... The bustling Champion Street.
232:And in the distance?
233:Well... it looks dark and cold compared to where the festivities are.
234:That's why... we must let the lights stretch out from Champion Street until they fill all of One Han City.
235:And from One Han City, they will light paths to every single place.
236:Fuuka turns her head to look at me. I don't know if it's the drunken haze or the warm light, but some of her queenly demeanor has fallen away to reveal more of a gentle side than usual.
237:The celebration was a success. Your contributions are undeniable.
238:The truth is, I didn't expect you to ace so many tasks in such a short amount of time.
239:In the end, we didn't even need the five or six backup plans I had Ume prepare for you. Hehe.
240:Honestly, that's mainly because everyone else has done such a good job. I just tried to keep apace.
241:And you know how to charm people with sweet talk. Well, I hope you'll keep up the good work, my new secretary.
242:Relax.
243:She reaches out and clasps my shoulders firmly with both hands.
244:One day, you'll have your place in Bamboo Cloud too.
245:Her face lights up when she says this. I look in the direction she pointed just now, then further into the distance... A glimmer of hope also sparks in my heart--If it's Fuuka, I may not have to wait too long.
246:The fiery liquid runs down my throat and into my stomach, and my vision begins to blur.
247:Whoops! I forgot to say, this wine is called "broken osmanthus branch," and it's quite strong.
248:And you just gulped it all down, tsk tsk...
249:...
250:Lemme see...
251:Fuuka Minami sways back and forth before my eyes... Finally, I can't suppress the intoxication any longer, and everything goes dark.
252:Upward management... unsuccessful...
